@madhusofficial in Mayfair has introduced their High Chai afternoon tea. I really am not just saying this but I genuinely was super impressed with the food. We chose the non vegetarian High Chai, as it’s fully halal! the sandwiches were filling like the Tandoori Salmon and Chilli Lemon and Chicken Wraps. 

The other savouries were the mini lamb burger, prawn toast and the flavoursome paneer and daal tartlet! Honestly there was so much to get through! 

The Mango Posset was a wow sweet treat for us, and the Tandoori Chai was fresh, warm and had all the right blend of spices! The scones were ok, I didn’t feel they were made on site and the jam that came with it wasn’t great, but for £38pp this afternoon tea which allows you to replenish items was incredible value for Mayfair! The quality of the items were very good! I’ve been to other Indian afternoon teas which have been double the price and no where near the quality and grandeur we received at Madhus. I will definitely be back. Staff were polite and professional and made our experience enjoyable. #invite #halalfoodlondon #indianafternoontea #afternoontea #londonafternoontea #mayfair #halalfoodie #londonfood #halalfoodblog #londonfoodblog #highchai #afternoontealondon

